# Corpus unit what-will-my-model-forget/C03 — gap (mandatory power CQ unmet; graded predicate dropped)
#
# Source: m0/annotations/what-will-my-model-forget.yaml C03 (negative-result,
# controlled_comparison; corpus pin 62e9b54). Headline: logit-change-transfer forecasting is
# partially interpretable and beats the tuned threshold on BART0 but FAILS on FLAN-T5 — trainable
# logit F1 57.15 vs threshold 55.75 on BART0Large/Full FT, but 36.54 vs 43.93 on FLAN-T5Large/LoRA
# and 40.91 vs 48.43 on FLAN-T5Large/Full FT (E01/E02, Table 1, section 5.1).
#
# Lowering notes (conventions: corpus-units/LOWERING.md):
#   * Negative-result claim: the headline outcome by precedence is the FLAN-T5 FAILURE, which is
#     genuinely the negation of a comparison, so it lowers through the `null_comparison` dual ->
#     conclusion not_better(trainable_logit, threshold, forecasting_f1, flan_t5_configs). Per the
#     no-both-sides rule, only the negative (FLAN-T5) side is argued; the BART0 win (a `better`
#     conclusion, the opposite contrary) stays in nl and refs, so no mutual rebut edges are forced.
#   * Graded/undefined-predicate flag (kind-b wishlist, annotation-summary §3): "partially
#     interpretable" is a graded property of the method with no construct in the vocabulary. It is
#     resolved by binding discipline — the formal atom uses precise constants over the F1 ordering
#     only, and the interpretability qualifier is carried by the nl hedge, dropping out of the
#     formalization as the annotation's coverage flag directs.
#   * null_comparison's mandatory adequate_power CQ (powered) maps onto the annotation's mandatory
#     "are the three deciding cell values reported with seeds or uncertainty?" — annotated
#     unmet-gap (single-run F1; the BART0 margin is 1.4 points with no variance). An open mandatory
#     obligation is IncompleteArgument, so NO complete arg is declarable: E2-style gap.
#   * baseline_parity (threshold tuned per config) and measurement_validity (one E01 pipeline,
#     binary F1) are annotated met and their leaves are supplied. The FLAN-T5 mechanism-diagnosis
#     CQ and the E02 transfer-scale CQ are further unmet CQs carried by the nl hedge.
#   * Leaf kinds are attested (Table 1 cells cited via trace N07/N08, read from the paper's table).
#
# Expected verdict is at the bottom of this file (golden oracle).

artifact what-will-my-model-forget at sha256:d5369ef41c64
policy corpus-v1
use backends [nd@1]

# --- The headline claim, the FLAN-T5 failure conjunct ------------------------------------------

claim c03
  nl      = "Trainable logit-change forecasting beats the tuned threshold on BART0Large Full FT (57.15 vs 55.75) but loses on FLAN-T5Large LoRA (36.54 vs 43.93) and Full FT (40.91 vs 48.43), a partially interpretable method that fails to transfer to FLAN-T5; the deciding cells are single runs and the kernel-capacity explanation is not diagnosed"
  formal  = not_better(trainable_logit, threshold, forecasting_f1, flan_t5_configs)
  binding = { author = m0-annotator, audit-status = unreviewed }

# --- Evidence leaves are present ... ------------------------------------------------------------

# Principal premise: the two FLAN-T5 Table 1 cell pairs where threshold beats trainable logit,
# per result cell, with the BART0 win folded into refs.
leaf e1 : reports(e01, compares(trainable_logit, threshold, forecasting_f1, flan_t5_configs, null))
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/claims.md#C03, logic/experiments.md#E01, trace/exploration_tree.yaml#N08, Table-1]

leaf e2 : matched_setup(trainable_logit, threshold, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Baselines, logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure]

leaf e3 : valid_measurement(forecasting_f1, e01)
  kind       = attested
  provenance = ai-executed
  refs       = [logic/experiments.md#E01-Procedure, logic/experiments.md#E01-Metrics]

# --- ... but no complete argument is declarable -------------------------------------------------

# (Intentionally no `arg`: powered(e01) has no honest leaf — single-run F1 per deciding cell, no
# seeds or uncertainty — and null_comparison makes that obligation mandatory. The FLAN-T5
# mechanism diagnosis is a further unmet mandatory CQ. The complete-support set is empty.)

status c03

